        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The AR350 and AR500 are the same solvent-based acrylic in two sheens. Foundation Armor's own data sheets give them the same solids, coverage, cure times and lifespan claim, so the choice comes down to how much gloss your surface can carry and how often people walk on it wet.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most stamped patios, pool decks, walkways and driveways, buy the AR350 and add non-slip where feet meet water. Save the AR500 for smooth, covered or showpiece surfaces where the shine is the point, and test both on a corner of your own slab before you buy by the pail.
          </p>
